WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:03.840
While HAX is great for text editing, the

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:05.920
real power of the system is shown

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:08.120
through its blocks engine.

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:10.400
To access the blocks menu,

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:13.640
click edit.

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:15.440
Then select blocks if it's not already

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:16.800
selected,

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:19.280
and you'll see the entire blocks panel.

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:21.560
So, from here we can either upload media

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:25.680
directly to have it inserted as a block.

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:28.400
We can view some popular blocks hovering

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:30.400
over them in order to see a preview of

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:33.480
what it'll be.

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:35.680
As we add blocks, they'll accumulate in

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:38.920
our recents tab, and we can also

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:41.240
expand and see all of the different

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:43.800
blocks that exist. It's

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:46.000
almost overwhelming how many blocks we

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:48.280
support in the system, and it's an

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:51.200
ever-expanding universe.

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:53.960
A common block to add would definitely

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:55.560
be

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:58.200
video or anything beyond the initial

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:01.840
text blocks.

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:03.840
By hitting filter content type, I can

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:06.040
type video,

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:07.360
and see all of the things that could

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:09.520
potentially play video in this case, a

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:11.440
media playlist.

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:14.600
So, from there I can drag that item into

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:17.040
the page, or I can just

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:18.840
press the button to insert it wherever

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:21.560
is active.

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:24.720
Every block that gets inserted in HAX

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:27.480
relates back to a sustainable

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:29.680
HTML tag.

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:31.640
In this case, a media playlist, which

00:01:31.640 --> 00:01:35.160
has a video player in it.

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:37.280
The beauty of the HAX system, though, is

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:38.920
that you shouldn't have to look at the

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:42.520
HTML, though it's always there to help.

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:44.480
If I want to reposition this block, I

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:46.760
can grab the drag handle,

00:01:46.760 --> 00:01:48.280
select the area that I want to drop it

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:50.720
into the page,

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:53.320
or hover over and just tell it to move

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:58.160
up or down one, depending on where I am.

00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:00.680
When I'm ready, I can hit save.

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:02.280
And now that block is there to be

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:04.280
presented to our users.
